          "at": "2026-07-05T03:21:27.169179+00:00",
          "body": "**Albanese-subproject dimension (T13 write scope covers both trees) \u2014 the bigger carve lives here.**\n\nThe AJC/Albanese `WeilDivisor.lean` copies have **diverged**, and the Albanese one drags a much larger genus-0 tail:\n\n- AJC `RiemannRoch/WeilDivisor.lean` imports `AlgebraicJacobian.Genus` + `Albanese.CoheightBridge` (no `Genus0BaseObjects`).\n- **Albanese** `RiemannRoch/WeilDivisor.lean` imports `AlgebraicJacobian.Genus0BaseObjects`, and is itself imported only by `Albanese/CodimOneExtension.lean` (live `ALB.codim1`).\n- The whole **`Genus0BaseObjects/` tree** (`BareScheme`, `ChartIso`, `Points`, `Cross01Substrate`, `GmScaling` \u2014 the `\u2119\u00b9`/`Ga`/`Gm` construction, ~13 `sorry`) survives **only in the Albanese subproject**, and is imported by nothing except that `WeilDivisor.lean`.\n\n**Consequence:** the dual-purpose carve of Albanese's `WeilDivisor` (keep `PrimeDivisor`/`order`, drop the degree/RR\u2192\u2119\u00b9 block per I-0106) also removes the `import Genus0BaseObjects`, orphaning the entire tree \u2014 collapsing ~13 `sorry` and ~100 Albanese blueprint nodes keyed on `def:genus0_base_objects` / `Genus0BaseObjects/*.lean`. That is the main Albanese deliverable of T13.\n\n**Housekeeping residue (not source):** stale generated `blueprint/web/chap-Genus0BaseObjects_*.html` + `.lake` build artifacts persist in the AJC tree even though the AJC `Genus0BaseObjects` source is already gone; harmless, regenerated. The AJC **structured** blueprint JSON is already genus-0-clean; the Albanese blueprint JSON still carries the ~100 genus-0 nodes.\n\nNet: keep both `WeilDivisor` copies in sync after the carve, and re-`lake build` **both** AJC and Albanese to confirm `CodimOneExtension` still compiles."
